The start is 8.
The queue is an empty list of whole numbers.
The distances is an empty list of whole numbers.
The seen is an empty list of whole numbers.
Place start into queue.
Place 0 into distances.
Place start into seen.
The head is 0.
The depth is 1.
The answer is 0.
The found is 0.
Repeat while head is less than depth and found is 0.
The current is item head of queue.
The steps is item head of distances.
Add 1 to head.
The parity is current modulo 2.
The chosen is current minus 1.
The upper is current plus 1.
If parity is 0, set chosen to current divided by 2.
If chosen is 1, set answer to steps plus 1, set found to 1.
If chosen is more than 1, if seen does not contain chosen, Place chosen into queue, Place (steps plus 1) into distances, Place chosen into seen, add 1 to depth.
If parity is 1, if upper is 1, set answer to steps plus 1, set found to 1.
If parity is 1, if upper is more than 1, if seen does not contain upper, Place upper into queue, Place (steps plus 1) into distances, Place upper into seen, add 1 to depth.

Show answer.
